# Git Flow Governance Rule

## Branching policy
- Do not commit directly to protected branches (`main`, `master`, `release/*`).
- Use short-lived working branches with clear names:
  - `feature/<work-item>-<short-title>`
  - `fix/<work-item>-<short-title>`
  - `chore/<short-title>`

## Pull request policy
- Every non-trivial change must go through a PR.
- PR must include scope summary, risk notes, and evidence paths.
- PR must pass required checks (build/test/security) before merge.
- PR must have required review approvals for the repository policy.

## Merge policy
- Prefer squash merge for feature/fix branches unless repository policy says otherwise.
- Do not force-push protected branches.
- Resolve review comments before final merge.

## Release safety
- No merge to protected branch when critical defects or security blockers remain open.
- QC Go/No-Go evidence is required for release-impacting changes.
